            <ArticleTitle>[Acute abdomen due to eosinophilic gastroenteritis. A study of 2 cases].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>204-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Report of two cases of eosinophilic gastroenteritis. In both cases the presentation was an acute abdomen syndrome. The etiological diagnosis was postoperative, because in the preoperative period there were no data characteristic of this entity. Probably this disease is more frequent than reported and although the treatment is medical, there are some cases in which surgery is justified.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
